[{"id":95293,"sender_id":868,"sender_full_name":"YimingXu","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e11f8d04f6e69478b34e292f6490725d?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/How.20can.20the.20Cartesian.20product.20serve.20as.20the.20coproduct.20in.20Rel.E2.80.A6/near/95293\">#1</a> Hi, all.</p>\n<p>I am reading the SEAR nlab page here: https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/SEAR</p>\n<p>Regarding Theorem 2.8, it says:</p>\n<p>Theorem 2.8. For any sets A and B, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A\\times B</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span></span></span></span> is a product of A and B in the category Set, and a coproduct in the category Rel.</p>\n<p>and the proofs says just in naive set theory. </p>\n<p>But the coproduct of Rel in naive set theory is the disjoint union! I am confused how can <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A\\times B</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span></span></span></span> can serve as the coproduct of Rel, I know that the coproduct/product in Rel is the disjoint union, but how can the cartesian product coincide with the disjoint union? Given relation <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>X</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f:A\\to X,g:B\\to X</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">:</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">:</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span></span></span></span>, how can we define the relation <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A \\times B \\to X</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span></span></span></span> so it is a coproduct?</p>\n<p>I assume the inclusion relations <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A\\to A \\times B</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B\\to A\\times B</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span></span></span></span> is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(a,(a1,b1))</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">))</span></span></span></span> holds iff <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a = a1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>, and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(b,(a1,b1))</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">))</span></span></span></span> holds iff <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b = b1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>. I may also make mistake here but I still wonder what else could it be. </p>\n<p>Thank you for any explaination! (and sorry if it turns out to be a stupid question…)</p>","timestamp":1636966161,"subject":"How can the Cartesian product serve as the coproduct in Rel…","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":95294,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/How.20can.20the.20Cartesian.20product.20serve.20as.20the.20coproduct.20in.20Rel.E2.80.A6/near/95294\">#2</a> Not to answer your question (i have never worked on or even read that page) but just to note that in order to hyperlink to an entry here, just enclose its name in double square brackets: <code>[[SEAR]]</code> produces <em><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/SEAR\">SEAR</a></em>. Specifically, you are asking about <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/SEAR#product\">this Prop.</a>.</p>\n<p>Hm, but looking at what it says there, I agree that it <em>sounds</em> like directly contradicting both what one expects as well as what it says at <em><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Rel\">Rel</a></em> (<a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Rel#LimitsAndColimit\">here</a>). Maybe a typo.</p>","timestamp":1636966970,"subject":"How can the Cartesian product serve as the coproduct in Rel…","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":95296,"sender_id":868,"sender_full_name":"YimingXu","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e11f8d04f6e69478b34e292f6490725d?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/How.20can.20the.20Cartesian.20product.20serve.20as.20the.20coproduct.20in.20Rel.E2.80.A6/near/95296\">#3</a> Thanks for the quick reply and comment anyway, and thank you for teaching me to write the link.</p>\n<p>By the way, I think I can report a typo now in a relative page <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/allegory\">allegory</a>, in the subsection <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/allegory%23division-allegory\">allegory#division-allegory</a>, I saw:</p>\n<p>That is: given <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r:A\\to B</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">:</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s:A\\to C</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">:</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span></span></span></span>, there exists <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r/s:B\\to C</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">:</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span></span></span></span> such that <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t\\le s/r\\in {\\mathrm{hom}}(B,C)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7719em;vertical-align:-0.136em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≤</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">hom</span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>…</p>\n<p>It seems that the first <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r/s</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span></span></span></span> should be <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s/r</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span></span></span></span>.</p>","timestamp":1636968072,"subject":"How can the Cartesian product serve as the coproduct in Rel…","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":95297,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/How.20can.20the.20Cartesian.20product.20serve.20as.20the.20coproduct.20in.20Rel.E2.80.A6/near/95297\">#4</a> If you spot typos and think you know what you are doing, then you are doing the community a favor by going ahead and fixing them. Thanks!</p>","timestamp":1636969594,"subject":"How can the Cartesian product serve as the coproduct in Rel…","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":95298,"sender_id":26,"sender_full_name":"Guest","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/70047463d6cf7b6f06d335988676e2aa?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/How.20can.20the.20Cartesian.20product.20serve.20as.20the.20coproduct.20in.20Rel.E2.80.A6/near/95298\">#5</a> Re <a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/How.20can.20the.20Cartesian.20product.20serve.20as.20the.20coproduct.20in.20Rel.E2.80.A6/near/95293\">#1</a>: For a non-naïve set theory proof that <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/SEAR/55#product\">theorem 2.8</a> is wrong: <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Rel\">Rel</a> is the <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Kleisli%20category\">Kleisli category</a> of the power set monad, so the inclusion <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{Set}\\to\\mathrm{Rel}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Set</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Rel</span></span></span></span></span> <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/monad%23RelationToAdjunctionsAndMonadicity\">preserves colimits</a>, but the product set <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A\\times B</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span></span></span></span> and disjoint union set <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊔</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A\\sqcup B</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⊔</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span></span></span></span> are generally not isomorphic in Rel since they needn’t have the same cardinality (and invertible relations are <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/bicategory%20of%20maps\">functions</a>).\n(That <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊔</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A\\sqcup B</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⊔</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span></span></span></span> is also the product in Rel follows from <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Rel</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>⊔</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≅</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Set</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>×</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>⊔</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≅</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Set</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>⊔</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≅</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Set</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>A</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Set</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>B</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≅</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Rel</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Rel</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Rel}(X,A\\sqcup B)\n\\cong\\operatorname{Set}(X\\times (A\\sqcup B),\\Omega)\n\\cong\\operatorname{Set}((X\\times A)\\sqcup (X\\times B),\\Omega)\n\\cong\\operatorname{Set}(X\\times A,\\Omega)\\times\\operatorname{Set}(X\\times B,\\Omega)\n\\cong\\operatorname{Rel}(X,A)\\times\\operatorname{Rel}(X,B)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Rel</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⊔</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Set</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⊔</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Ω</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Set</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">((</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⊔</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Ω</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Set</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Ω</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Set</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Ω</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Rel</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Rel</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>.)</p>\n<p>The disjoint union of sets isn’t introduced until later on in the article, so I’ll just remove the mention of Rel from the theorem.</p>","timestamp":1636977985,"subject":"How can the Cartesian product serve as the coproduct in Rel…","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":95332,"sender_id":868,"sender_full_name":"YimingXu","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e11f8d04f6e69478b34e292f6490725d?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/How.20can.20the.20Cartesian.20product.20serve.20as.20the.20coproduct.20in.20Rel.E2.80.A6/near/95332\">#6</a> Thank you, then I will just skip it. And thanks for the explanation above!</p>\n<p>But I am still interested in what is the intended theorem there. If someone knows, thanks for telling me or just editing the page…</p>","timestamp":1637284064,"subject":"How can the Cartesian product serve as the coproduct in Rel…","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":95336,"sender_id":10,"sender_full_name":"Mike Shulman","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ede34282f405f902e12fa7e6cf336572?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/How.20can.20the.20Cartesian.20product.20serve.20as.20the.20coproduct.20in.20Rel.E2.80.A6/near/95336\">#7</a> I expect this was just a mistake.  Whoever wrote that (probably me) may have been thinking of the fact that, as mentioned above, the coproduct in Set is both a product and a coproduct in Rel, and mistakenly dualized it.</p>","timestamp":1637337424,"subject":"How can the Cartesian product serve as the coproduct in Rel…","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]}]